1	// LockstepSession (cosim_redesign F4): the vsim side of lock-step DV
2	// co-sim. The whole session is DMI-driven -- halt at reset, single-step to
3	// the arm pc, then one drain_full record per execution attempt -- so record
4	// boundaries are exact (no haltreq slack) and traps align by construction:
5	// a step that traps re-enters debug mode at the handler entry, which is
6	// exactly where the QEMU oracle's next pre-execution callback drains.
